WEB SOURCE (the specification — read end to end)
  web/src/features/vehicles/components/VehicleCharts.tsx — a presentational component (props
  state / positions / vehicleConfigData / userPrefData; hooks useTranslation + useUnits) rendering a
  responsive grid (grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2) of FOUR GlassPanels:
    1. Location (web `{state.latitude && state.longitude && ...}`): a Leaflet MapContainer centred on
       the live position with a vehicle Marker, a trail Polyline (positions filtered by
       `p.latitude && p.longitude`), a MapLayerSwitcher, and a monospaced `fmtNumber(lat), fmtNumber(lon)`
       footer. Title t('common.location').
    2. Vehicle Configuration (web `{vehicleConfigData && ...}`): 18 <MetricCard> cells —
       cleanNil(...) || '—' for the strings, `!= null ? (Yes/No | Active/Off | Present/No) : '—'` for
       the booleans, `${pct}%` for the SW download/install, sunroof || 'Not Installed',
       swUpdate || 'None'. Title t('common.vehicleConfig'); lucide Car.
    3. Car Display Preferences (web `{userPrefData && ...}`): a note paragraph + 5 <MetricCard> cells
       via parseSettingEnum (distance/temperature/charge/pressure) + the 24h-time Yes/No.
       Title t('common.carPreferences'); lucide Settings.
    4. Speed History (always): a Recharts AreaChart of
       `batteryData = positions.map(p -> { time: formatTime(p.ts),
        speed: p.speed_mph != null ? convertSpeedFromSI(p.speed_mph, unitPrefs.speed) : null }).reverse()`,
       else the empty copy t('common.positionDataWillAppear'). Title t('common.speedHistory'); lucide Activity.
  Helpers reproduced verbatim (arithmetic is the contract): convertSpeedFromSI (km/h = mps*3600/1000;
  mph = mps*3600/1609.344), fmtNumber (locale grouping, default precision 2, safeNumber 0), cleanNil
  ('' / '<nil>' / 'nil' / 'null' ⇒ absent), parseSettingEnum (lower-case + strip non-alpha, map; unknown
  ⇒ raw; nil ⇒ '—'), formatTime (short locale time). The `speed_mph` JSON key carries SI m/s — the
  ADR-004 telemetry naming paradox; the producer delivers SI and the renderer converts at the boundary.
  i18n: the web source mixes t() keys (common.location/vehicleConfig/carPreferences/speedHistory,
  vehicles.detail.europeVehicle/rhd, common.yes/no, common.positionDataWillAppear) with hardcoded
  English literals (every config / preference label + value). Per the native no-English-literals rule
  every literal is promoted to a key (table "VehicleCharts").

