STATES (every one renders — no hidden surface)
  loading  → skeleton section panels (P4 leaf; the web is presentational).
  empty    → no data in any section → one friendly message, never a blank box.
  error    → retryable error chrome (P4 leaf; the web has no error branch).
  data     → the four sections, each rendering its content OR a friendly per-section empty state. The
             web HIDES absent sections (`{vehicleConfigData && ...}`); per ADR-011 / prohibited-pattern
             #6 the native leaf never hides a surface — it shows a placeholder instead (a sanctioned
             superset, never a narrowing). The speed section's empty stands in for the web
             "Position data will appear here" (and for an all-null series, which would render a blank
             chart — a more covenant-compliant empty than an axes-only box).
  stale    → header chip + banner + one-shot auto-refresh on the live→stale transition.
  offline  → header chip + banner over last-known content; no auto-refresh.

